      "writtenOn": "2014-11-12T16:08:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No but the spec \"lawyers\" and my co-workers decided that the 500mA entry was not mandatory/not useful, the vSafe5V entry is now 3A on our chargers.\n\nBy the way we can go even lower if we don\u0027t plan to suck any current : 10mA",
      "parentUuid": "5aabf756_3a77a5fd",
      "revId": "855e0c973aa7e4c5e06b8f9da3e2ae2196e0ed17",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3aa8035b_0dd71952",
        "filename": "board/samus_pd/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1103909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-11-12T16:24:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem with going below 500mA is that the EC has a minimum input current limit of 500mA (which is actually limited by problems with the charging circuit at lower current draws). So, if charge manager switches to start charging from this port, it will draw 500mA minimum.",
      "parentUuid": "5aabf756_5a63813c",
      "revId": "855e0c973aa7e4c5e06b8f9da3e2ae2196e0ed17",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
